      "html" : "<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182963\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182963\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFor SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 pound per foot = 14.59 N\/m.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182964\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182964\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta.&#160;&#160;&#160;Values are not cumulative with other horizontal diaphragm values and are for short-term wind or seismic loading. Values shall be reduced 25 percent for normal loading.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182965\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182965\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tb.&#160;&#160;&#160;Values shall be reduced 50 percent in Seismic Design Categories D, E and F.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182966\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182966\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tc.&#160;&#160;&#160;1 1\/4-inch, No. 6 Type S or W screws are permitted to be substituted for the listed nails.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
      "id" : "19011-html-3",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 pound per foot = 14.59 N\/m.\n\n a. Values are not cumulative with other horizontal diaphragm values and are for short-term wind or seismic loading. Values shall be reduced 25 percent for normal loading.\n\n b. Values shall be reduced 50 percent in Seismic Design Categories D, E and F.\n\n c. 1 1\/4-inch, No. 6 Type S or W screws are permitted to be substituted for the listed nails."
